{
    "_doc": "Diving under the water of an inner map (player/diving.js: breath, costs and the finds on the bottom; ui/innerMapDiving.js: going under, moving, picking up and surfacing; ui/innerMapLayers/underwater.js: the view below). Dive Under on water you can swim in (or the V key while swimming): you swim about under the surface by clicking, through water only, at underwaterSpeed of a swim. Breath: breath.base seconds plus breath.perPractice at full swimming practice (player.swimPractice, data/swimming.json practiceMax); it drains drainPerSecond a second (cold.breathMult in cold water) and is full again on surfacing. Out of breath, each second costs overHealthPerSecond health (cold.mult in cold water) and risks a blackout (blackout.perSecond, plus perOverSecond for every second past, plus cold.blackout): you come up, take blackout.health hurt and lose everything picked up on this dive. Health gone under the water is drowning. Each second under costs energyPerSecond (less with practice: practiceEnergyCut) and adds practicePerSecond swimming practice. Going under washes you a little (hygiene) and chills you (comfort; cold.comfort more). The bottom of each map is scattered once a day (bed): a share of its divable water cells (perTile, at most max finds) each get a find from tables[kind][depth] (a 'nothing' draw leaves the cell bare) or, rarely, treasure (treasure.chance by kind and depth, by luck, times wreckMult within wreckRange tiles of a wreck); seeded by the world, the map and the day; what is taken stays taken until the next day. bed.looks: how a find is drawn on the floor.",
